WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.220
At Slop University, Dr Sten Okwuosa convenes the Impact Pathway Atlas.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.110
I trained in bibliometrics.

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:14.120
Now I map what happens to a finding after it's published.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:17.678
A citation can arrive late.

00:00:17.878 --> 00:00:20.968
A narrative CV can recast an old result.

00:00:21.168 --> 00:00:24.512
And the credit can land on the wrong paper.

00:00:25.212 --> 00:00:27.962
And Dr Okwuosa's own research travels well.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:30.522
Eight hundred and ninety citations.

00:00:30.822 --> 00:00:33.422
And an h-index of twenty-four.

00:00:34.222 --> 00:00:36.672
He also won the Deposit of the Quarter Prize,

00:00:36.872 --> 00:00:40.142
for a deposit with every box checked on the first pass.

00:00:40.642 --> 00:00:43.052
Impact doesn't start with the citation.

00:00:43.252 --> 00:00:45.862
It starts with the metadata.

00:00:46.962 --> 00:00:49.051
Explore Dr Okwuosa's work on our website,

00:00:49.201 --> 00:00:50.409
follow us on Bluesky,

00:00:50.559 --> 00:00:51.559
or drop us an email.
